 "result_text": "I fixed the bad fractional part in `pysubs2/substation.py` (`ms_to_timestamp`). I checked it with a quick call to `ms_to_timestamp`, not the full test suite. A time of 4659995 ms (1:17:39.995) now gives `1:17:40.00`.\n\nThe old code split the time into hours, minutes, seconds and milliseconds first, then rounded the milliseconds to centiseconds. Anything from .995 to .999 rounded up to 100 centiseconds and printed as `.100` instead of carrying into the next second. The fix rounds the whole time to the nearest centisecond first and only then splits it, so the carry works.\n\nI didn't run your `--shift-back 1045ms` command on the example file.",
